<title>UK: UK's Channel 5 names ex-YTV exec as head of sport.</title>
<headline>UK's Channel 5 names ex-YTV exec as head of sport.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>British television upstart Channel 5 said on Tuesday it named former Yorkshire Television executive Robert Charles as its new controller of sport to help boost its sports coverage.</p>
<p>Charles will succeed Nick Wilson, who will concentrate on expanding the channel's children's output.</p>
<p>Charles was formerly controller of sport at Yorkshire Television.</p>
<p>Channel 5, owned in part by United News &amp; Media Plc and Pearson Plc, was launched earlier this year to compete with Britain's four other terrestrial TV channels. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
